    "message": "Symbian: apply cached native SDK patches as a verified stack\n\nCI44 restored a complete converter source cache, but an early patch's reverse\ncheck failed after later patches had changed its context. Reapplying that\nalready-present patch aborted the E32 converter step before any SIS was built.\n\nCompute every ordered prefix from v0.3.0 in a temporary Git index/object store,\nrecognize all patch-owned files by contents and mode, apply only a known prefix's\nremaining changes, and verify the complete final postimage. Preserve unrelated\nlocal/staged edits and the real index; refuse unknown or partial owned-file\nchanges without reset/clean. Repeat the helper after native build/tests so a\nfresh CI cache miss also covers the already-patched path.\n\nRoot's real six-patch fixture regression passes all 11 tests, including prefixes\n1-5, complete repeat, the previous reverse-check failure, preserved user edits\nand index, partial/conflicting/missing states and symlink refusal. Shell syntax\nand owned-source cached checks pass. Retain CI44 failure and repair evidence;\nverbatim SDK references retain their original whitespace and hashes.",
    "timestamp": "2026-11-01T06:01:30Z",
